  "scope": "# Review \u2014 task 36275402c6b2\nTask/source: assignment `review-7c7b4b0c0be9c4da`; approved generator v4.1.0, SHA-256 `b65d3ab83f95f86f64fee72b91222edf31101a70fb7e1770acaf67b5befc0c58`, rule hash `08894540e7f2`.\nDefect \u2192 repair: the requested small parametric extension was missing; I built a source-bound, unapproved `border_policy={recolour,preserve}` prototype, focused tests, and a reusable replay/tamper verifier.\nChecks actually run: staged baseline 29/29; final focused prototype/verifier 16/16; final staged suite 45/45; both Racket programs, all retained episodes, and all five labeled canonical pairs replayed.\nRemaining failures: none in the final receipts. Historical red tests and one raw-pytest namespace diagnostic are retained as evidence, not relabeled as final failures.\nRemaining limits: one noncorner border source per input, two declared policies, and finite seeds; corner/multiple-border witnesses and arbitrary rival programs remain outside scope.\nReference-rule change: none. Canonical `recolour` Racket source remains byte-identical at SHA-256 `a806f83cdfb3f7831cfe4c189fee46cdc90677706f05b67cb617dafc2b080f86`.\nDisposition: routine owner review of a verified proposal; no production integration, approval, audit clearing, or training admission is asserted.\nSupplementary tickets: both bounded tickets completed; the peer audit witness reproduced and remains open.\n\n## Built artifact\n",
